  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "---\ndescription: \"Optional bundle for adding and managing MCP servers through profile patches.\"\nkind: \"package-bundle\"\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "`@tinyforge/dsh-mcp-settings`",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nAn optional DSH bundle for configuring Streamable HTTP and stdio MCP servers from DSH Settings."
    },
    {
      "section": "Quick start",
      "text": "From the directory containing this checkout, adjust the local path if your checkout folder has a different name:\n\n```sh\npnpm dsh plugin --profile <profile> add file:./dsh-mcp-settings\n```\n\nThen open **Settings → MCP Servers** to add a server or import a configuration."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- Configure Streamable HTTP and stdio MCP servers.\n- Import Streamable HTTP entries from an `mcpServers` JSON object.\n- Search and filter servers by name, connection state, and transport; inspect tool names and descriptions while connected.\n- Preview JSON imports before saving, and reveal individual secret fields only when needed.\n- Export managed settings as JSON. Credential values stay in the local credential store and must be configured separately in another profile.\n- Store sensitive headers, including `Authorization`, in DSH's credential store.\n- Check a server connection before saving its settings.\n- Get fixed next-step guidance for authorization failures, connection failures, and timeouts.\n- Keep `project-memory` servers separate from model-facing tools."
    },
    {
      "section": "Runtime behavior",
      "text": "The default server list is empty. Installing the bundle does not preconfigure or start an MCP service. Configured servers start when the profile loads. Only successfully connected servers with purpose `model-tools` publish tools to the model; `project-memory` servers remain with their registered consumer."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility and implementation",
      "text": "This release requires DSH `0.2.2-alpha.2` or a later stable `0.2.x` release. The MCP client runtime is included under `vendor/`. The bundle disables the built-in MCP settings page, adds the managed server manager, and exports Host Typert metadata for connection checks. The base MCP client provides live connection status."
    },
    {
      "section": "Import limitation",
      "text": "JSON import accepts Streamable HTTP entries in an `mcpServers` object or managed server entries in a `servers` array. Add stdio servers from the settings form or import them in the managed format. Entries with duplicate names are skipped."
    }
  ],
